## Aptitude vs Access

### Not Everyone Can Cast

**Natural magical aptitude is required** to:
- Sense magical fields
- Shape Intent properly
- Channel Intensity through your will
- Improvise and adapt spells in real-time

This is a talent, like perfect pitch or mathematical intuition. Some have it, most don't.

### Magical Devices Bypass Aptitude

**Anyone can use a wand, staff, or enchanted item:**
- The device handles the technical aspects
- User just needs to supply Intent (and sometimes energy)
- Pre-programmed effects, limited flexibility
- Traditional magical world relied on these for non-casters

**Technology becomes "our" version of magical devices:**
- A recording of the right frequencies = spell scroll
- A device programmed to produce harmonics = wand
- A "spell app" on a phone = grimoire
- Mass-produced access to magic

### The Three Classes

1. **Natural Casters** (rare)
   - Can sense and shape magic directly
   - Improvise and create new spells
   - Most powerful and flexible
   - Still benefit from tech amplification

2. **Device Users** (common)
   - No natural aptitude
   - Rely entirely on pre-made tools
   - Limited by their equipment
   - Can still be devastatingly effective

3. **Hybrid Users** (uncommon)
   - Some natural talent
   - Amplified by technology
   - Best of both worlds
   - Can modify and adapt device magic

