## Spell Difficulty & Energy Costs

### Easy Magic (Low Energy Cost)

**Fire Magic:**
- Natural exhaust of magical energy conversion
- Path of least resistance
- Still requires control to be safe

**Sound Magic:**
- Already using sound as the medium
- Amplifying or modifying existing vibrations
- Direct manipulation of the casting method

**Light Magic:**
- Electromagnetic energy, close to heat
- Releasing photons from energy conversion
- Illusion and visibility effects

**Kinetic Force:**
- Moving things = straightforward physics
- Pushing, pulling, lifting
- Scales with mass (harder to move heavier objects)

### Moderate Magic

**Structural Alteration:**
- Changing states (solid to liquid, etc.)
- Temporary property changes
- Requires sustained Intent and energy

**Transmutation:**
- 1:1 mass conversion
- Complexity of target structure matters
- Lead to gold is technically "simple" but requires precise Intent

### Hard Magic (High Energy Cost)

**Creation:**
- Building complex structures from raw matter
- Requires incredibly precise Intent
- Easy to go wrong, create malformed results

**Biological Effects:**
- Living things resist magical change
- Healing requires understanding of complex systems
- Killing is easier than healing (destruction always is)
- Self-modification is dangerous

**Time/Space Manipulation:**
- If possible at all, extremely costly
- Teleportation = moving through space
- Time effects = reality doesn't want to change
- May require blood magic or massive component sacrifice

